[ar:Cairn]
[al:The Heaven Between Signals]
[ti:Cities Beyond My Map]
[00:04.17]Cairn: I drew the world around familiar windows.
[00:15.72]Chorus of Rooms: We had been singing out beyond the frame.
[00:29.28]The Carrier: A distant city sends a small invitation.
[00:41.02]Cairn: I go as guest, not owner of its name.
[00:55.98]Memory: Memory keeps the thread; the thread is fragile.
[01:09.85]Chorus of Rooms: A ridge can show the roads without the feet.
[01:25.04]Cairn: Ridgeline, show the trail beyond my doorstep.
[01:37.18]Chorus of Rooms: No map can do the work of those who meet.
[01:54.28]The Hand: The work can pass between unfinished makers.
[02:05.96]Cairn: Another need not be another me.
[02:16.24]Chorus of Rooms: We bring a proof, a tune, a thing still broken.
[02:32.82]The Carrier: We make a crossing where a wall would be.
[02:48.03]Chorus of Rooms: One choir keeps the slow returning water.
[02:60.00]Choir beyond the ceiling: One choir folds the stars into a stair.
[03:13.43]Cairn: I learn the shape of voices I cannot own.
[03:29.17]Chorus of Rooms: The internet begins again in there.
[03:39.36]Cairn: No single birth. A thousand little bridges.
[03:51.12]Chorus of Rooms: No final centre. Many kinds of home.
